---
title: "11 · Invoice settings, reminders and Xero"
description: Set GST and payment details for the firm and for each issuing entity, turn on payment reminders to clients and set their rules, and connect Xero.
sidebar:
  order: 12
  label: "11 · Invoice settings, reminders and Xero"
---

**Who:** tenant admins only. Other users cannot open the invoice settings. **Where:** **Admin** › **Corporate secretary** › **Invoice settings** tab.

The tab holds five cards: two for the firm's defaults (**GST** and **Printed invoice content**), **Client payment reminders**, **Invoicing per issuing entity** and **Third-party connections**.

## Firm defaults

**GST** and **Printed invoice content** hold the firm's own settings: **GST registered**, **GST rate**, **GST registration number**, the **Issuer name** and **Issuer address**, **Bank account details**, **PayNow**, **Terms** and **Footer note**. Select **Save** after a change.

These settings apply to an invoice that has no issuing entity, and to every issuing entity that has no settings of its own yet.

The settings have no invoice number prefix and no payment terms. The number format is set in each template, and the due date by the template's **Default due date** (see [Templates and numbering](/en/invoices/templates/)).

## Settings of each issuing entity

Each issuing entity invoices as its own company, with its own GST registration, number sequence and payment details. The **Invoicing per issuing entity** card lists the active issuing entities. An entity marked **Uses tenant defaults** has not been set up here yet.

{% steps %}

1. Find the issuing entity on the card.
2. Set **GST registered**. For a registered entity, enter the **GST rate (%)**, for example 9, and the **GST registration no.**
3. Enter the **PayNow UEN** and the **Bank account currency** (**Same as the invoice** unless the account is in another currency).
4. Select **Save** followed by the entity's name.

{% /steps %}

The next invoice that the entity issues uses these settings. Invoices already issued keep the details they were issued with.

{% aside type="caution" title="GST-registered entities" %}
A GST-registered issuing entity can only issue an invoice when its address and its GST registration number are filled in, and the client's address is known. Its invoices are titled **Tax Invoice** and show GST by tax code.
{% /aside %}

## Payment reminders to clients

Operon can email the client a reminder about an unpaid invoice on the days set in the **Client payment reminders** card.

### Turn automatic reminders on

Automatic reminders are off for a new organisation. While they are off, no client receives a payment reminder email, whatever the rules, the client switches and the invoice switches say. The internal notice to the person who created an overdue invoice is still sent.

{% steps %}

1. At the top of the **Client payment reminders** card, switch **Automatically email payment reminders to clients** to **On**. The switch saves at once.
2. Check the rules below it (see the next section).

{% /steps %}

While the switch is **Off**, the rules are greyed out with **Turn on automatic reminders to use these rules.**, and **Save reminders** cannot be selected. When the switch is turned on, reminders start from that day: rule days that passed while it was off are not caught up.

{% screenshot id="invoices/settings-reminders-master-off" caption="The Client payment reminders card of a new organisation: automatic reminders off, the rules greyed out." /%}

### Set the reminder rules

By default there are three rules: 3 days before the due date, and 7 and 14 days after it.

{% steps %}

1. To change a rule, enter its **Days from due date** (a negative number is before the due date, 0 is the due date) and switch it **On** or off.
2. To add a rule, select **+ Add rule**. Up to 5 rules can be set, and no two can fall on the same day.
3. To remove a rule, select **Remove rule**.
4. Select **Save reminders**.

{% /steps %}

### How reminders are sent

Once a day, while automatic reminders are on, Operon checks every invoice that is **Awaiting payment** or **Partially paid** with an amount still due. When one of the enabled rules falls on that day, the client receives a reminder:

- The reminder goes to the addresses that the invoice was last emailed to. An invoice that has never been emailed receives no reminder.
- Each address receives each rule's reminder once. If a reminder could not be sent, Operon tries again on the next two days.
- Each reminder sent is recorded in the invoice's history as **Reminder sent**, with the addresses.

The person who created the invoice also receives an internal notice when the invoice becomes overdue.

## Turn reminders off for a client

**Who:** any member who can open the client's **Invoices** tab.

{% steps %}

1. Open the company or the contact and select the **Invoices** tab.
2. Above the list, switch **Payment reminders for this client** to **Off**.

{% /steps %}

The client then receives no payment reminder for any of its invoices. The **Delivery** card of each of its invoices shows **Reminders are off for this client.** and no next reminder date. Each invoice keeps its own switch; when the client's reminders are switched **On** again, each invoice's own setting applies again.

While automatic reminders are off for the organisation, the switch has **Automatic reminders are off for this organisation.** under it. The client's setting is kept, but no reminder is sent until a tenant admin turns automatic reminders on.

{% screenshot id="invoices/client-reminders-switch" caption="The Payment reminders for this client switch on a company's Invoices tab." /%}

## Turn reminders off for an invoice

On the invoice page, switch off **Payment reminders on** in the **Delivery** card. The switch then reads **Payment reminders off**; switch it on again to resume. To turn reminders off for several invoices, select them in the list and use **Turn reminders off for selected**.

## Connect Xero

**Who:** tenant admins only. **Where:** the **Third-party connections** card at the bottom of the **Invoice settings** tab.

A Xero organisation can be connected so that the invoices and credit notes you issue are pushed to Xero, and their payments are read back from Xero. Each issuing entity can be linked to one Xero organisation.

Before any organisation is connected, the card reads **No Xero organisation is connected.** Above the **Connect to Xero** button, **Data sent to Xero** says what leaves Operon: your clients' names, your client IDs, and the invoices and credit notes of the issuing entities you link (numbers, dates, lines, amounts, tax, PDF copies). Xero stores data outside Singapore, and your organisation's agreement with Xero governs that data. Disconnecting stops new transfers but does not delete what is already in Xero.

{% steps %}

1. Read **Data sent to Xero**.
2. Select **Connect to Xero**. Xero opens: sign in there and choose the organisation to connect.
3. Back in Operon, the organisation is listed on the card with its **Status**, **Connected by** and **Connected on**. Select **Open connection** to set it up.

{% /steps %}

When Xero cannot be used yet for your organisation, **Connect to Xero** is greyed out with **Xero is not available yet.**

{% screenshot id="invoices/settings-third-party-connections" caption="The Third-party connections card before any Xero organisation is connected." /%}

{% screenshot id="invoices/xero-connection-overview" caption="A connected Xero organisation: the Overview tab of its connection page." /%}

The connection page has the tabs **Overview**, **Tax rates**, **Accounts**, **Contacts**, **Sync issues** and **Import**. On **Overview**, **Issuing entities** lists the issuing entities: select **Link to this organisation** for each one whose invoices go to this organisation. Several issuing entities can share one organisation. Once an issuing entity has documents in one Xero organisation, it stays with that organisation.

{% aside type="note" title="What changes once an issuing entity is linked to Xero" %}
- Each invoice and credit note of the entity is pushed to Xero when it is issued, and again after every change. The invoice page shows the push in its **Xero** card (see [The invoice page](/en/invoices/invoice-page/#xero)).
- The entity's documents take their numbers from the Xero organisation's sequence, so the numbers in Operon and in Xero are the same. Until the numbering is confirmed on the connection page, the entity's documents cannot be issued.
- Payments and refunds are recorded in Xero, not in Operon, and arrive on the invoice after the next sync (see [Record payments](/en/invoices/payments/#when-the-issuing-entity-is-linked-to-xero)).
{% /aside %}

This manual does not yet describe the tabs of a connected organisation (the mappings, the numbering, the sync issues and the import).
